From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] replay: PLAY_REPLAY_SLOT plays from the frame it loads

PLAY_REPLAY_SLOT waits for the movie task, so the replay's initial
state is loaded while the command is handled, in the middle of an
iteration, before that iteration runs the core. The replay itself only
became the current one at the start of the next iteration. One frame
therefore ran on the loaded state with live input instead of the
replay's, and the playback followed the recording a frame late:
recorded on snes9x, every checkpoint of a Super Mario World replay
differed from the playback by a few hundred bytes of RAM, sound and
timer state. Recording starts between iterations, as playback from the
menu or a hotkey does, and has no such frame.

Make the replay current as soon as it is loaded.

Signed-off-by: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
---
--- a/command.c
+++ b/command.c
@@ -940,6 +940,11 @@
             snprintf(reply, sizeof(reply) - 1, "PLAY_REPLAY_SLOT %lld", (long long)(input_st->bsv_movie_state_next_handle->identifier));
          else
             snprintf(reply, sizeof(reply) - 1, "PLAY_REPLAY_SLOT 0");
+         /* The replay's state is in now, before this iteration runs the
+          * core, but a new replay only takes over at the start of the
+          * next one: this frame would run on the loaded state without
+          * the replay's input, and every frame after it one late. */
+         bsv_movie_dequeue_next(input_st);
          command_post_state_loaded();
       }
    }
